# Kessler — Controls

This file fixes the actions a player drives the game with, the keys bound to
each, and which actions each screen answers. The screens themselves are in
`specs/screens.md`, and the deflector rotation and ball launch the play
actions drive are in `specs/deflector-and-ball.md`. Kessler is keyboard only.

## How input reaches the game

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
This game stands on no engine, so the keyboard belongs to the runtime layer
you write. It binds keys by `KeyboardEvent.code`, so a binding is a physical
key whatever the keyboard layout, and it reports each action two ways: as a
held value, true while any of its keys is down, and as a press edge, true once
for the frame in which the held value became true. A key event whose `repeat`
flag is set arms no edge.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
The keyboard belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. The game registers the actions below
with the engine and reads each one every frame: the two rotation actions as
held values, and every other action as one press edge per press.
{{else}}
The keyboard belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. The game registers the actions below
with the engine, and the player controller the game mode adds is the one place
they are read: the two rotation actions as held values, and every other action
as one press edge per press.
{{/if}}

## The actions

`ACTIONS` holds the actions the game registers, and `BINDINGS` maps each to
the keys that fire it. A key is named by its `KeyboardEvent.code`, so the
bindings hold whatever keyboard layout the player types on.

| Action | Keys | Read as |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `left` | `ArrowLeft`, `KeyA` | held |
| `right` | `ArrowRight`, `KeyD` | held |
| `up` | `ArrowUp`, `KeyW` | edge |
| `down` | `ArrowDown`, `KeyS` | edge |
| `confirm` | `Space`, `Enter` | edge |
| `launch` | `Space` | edge |
| `back` | `Escape` | edge |
| `pause` | `KeyP` | edge |

The two keys bound to each rotation action are interchangeable: `KeyA` does
exactly what `ArrowLeft` does wherever `left` is read. `Space` carries both
`launch` and `confirm`, and the two never answer on the same screen. All
of a frame's edges are read against the screen the frame began on, so a
press that changes screens never also acts on the screen it lands in. The
debug overlay's backtick toggle is in `specs/instrumentation.md` and sits
outside the table.

## What each screen reads

| Screen | Live |
| --- | --- |
| `title` | `up` and `down` move the highlight; `confirm` accepts it. |
| `howto` | `confirm` and `back` return to `title`. |
| `playing` | `left`, `right`, `launch`, `back`, and `pause`. |
| `waveclear` | Nothing; the interstitial runs on its own timer. |
| `paused` | `up` and `down` move the highlight; `confirm` accepts it; `back` and `pause` resume. |
| `gameover` | `confirm` returns to `title`. |

An action a row omits does nothing on that screen.

On `playing`, `left` and `right` rotate the deflector along its track while
held, one per direction, at the rate `specs/deflector-and-ball.md` fixes;
`launch` launches the parked ball as the same file states; and `back` and
`pause` both pause, so a player reaches the pause menu with either `Escape` or
`KeyP`.

## Out of scope

- Touch and gamepad input. The game is played from the keyboard alone.
- Rebinding. The bindings are fixed and the game offers no way to change them.
